{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1708340,
  "courseSlug": "learn-flutter-dart-to-build-ios-android-apps",
  "courseTitle": "Flutter & Dart - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37143148",
      "title": "Using the Dismissible Widget for Dismissing List Items",
      "lectureOrder": 121,
      "videoOrder": 112,
      "sourceHash": "ff5c25b3be59087e4dab0a47ed3d6a0af762f74901d176c01fdc8a6d25bc00c5",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 4.26,
          "en": "So, this isn't looking too bad now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.26,
          "end": 9.26,
          "en": "We can now add new expenses here with amount, date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.39,
          "end": 11.16,
          "en": "category and a title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.16,
          "end": 14.07,
          "en": "Those expenses are then added to the list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.07,
          "end": 17.52,
          "en": "Of course, the styling as mentioned, isn't finalized yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.52,
          "end": 20.01,
          "en": "We'll take care about that soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.01,
          "end": 21.57,
          "en": "But before we do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.57,
          "end": 25.74,
          "en": "I wanna make sure that we can also get rid of expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.74,
          "end": 27.33,
          "en": "by swiping them away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.33,
          "end": 30.36,
          "en": "So by swiping from right to left.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.36,
          "end": 32.91,
          "en": "And at the moment, this is not possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.91,
          "end": 36.36,
          "en": "but it's such a common pattern that Flutter also helps a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.36,
          "end": 38.79,
          "en": "with implementing this pattern.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 41.4,
          "en": "So, how can we make sure that these items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.4,
          "end": 43.56,
          "en": "can be swiped away?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.56,
          "end": 46.8,
          "en": "Well, for that, we can go to our expenses_list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.8,
          "end": 50.85,
          "en": "where we have this ListView.builder with our expense items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.85,
          "end": 53.46,
          "en": "And Flutter gives us a special widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.46,
          "end": 58.32,
          "en": "which we can wrap around list items that should be swipeable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.32,
          "end": 62.4,
          "en": "or that should be dismissible, removable to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.4,
          "end": 67.4,
          "en": "And the widget conveniently is named Dismissible, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.06,
          "end": 70.89,
          "en": "Now Dismissible wants a child,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.89,
          "end": 74.52,
          "en": "and that should be the list item that can be swiped away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.52,
          "end": 79.52,
          "en": "So in my case, my ExpenseItem, but it then also needs a key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.64,
          "end": 82.68,
          "en": "And I mentioned this key before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.68,
          "end": 85.98,
          "en": "it was always this thing which we accepted here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.98,
          "end": 90.06,
          "en": "in our constructors and forwarded to the parent widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.06,
          "end": 93.63300000000001,
          "en": "And that was all we had to do with keys thus far.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.97999999999999,
          "end": 98.7,
          "en": "Now the good news is that in most cases, in most widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.7,
          "end": 101.49000000000001,
          "en": "that is all you have to do with keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.49000000000001,
          "end": 104.13,
          "en": "There is a good reason why we haven't seen keys",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.13,
          "end": 107.43,
          "en": "being used anywhere besides registering them here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.43,
          "end": 108.813,
          "en": "in our constructors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.87299999999999,
          "end": 112.17,
          "en": "But there sometimes are scenarios",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.17,
          "end": 114.24000000000001,
          "en": "where those keys are actually needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.24000000000001,
          "end": 117.9,
          "en": "because this key mechanism exists to make widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.9,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "uniquely identifiable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 122.76,
          "en": "And I'll dive a bit deeper into all of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.76,
          "end": 124.38,
          "en": "in a later section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 125.55,
          "en": "But in the end here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.55,
          "end": 129,
          "en": "where we should be able to swipe widgets away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129,
          "end": 132.78,
          "en": "and then remove the data that's associated with a widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.78,
          "end": 135.78,
          "en": "a key is needed to allow Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.78,
          "end": 139.2,
          "en": "to uniquely identify a widget and the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.2,
          "end": 140.763,
          "en": "that's associated with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.32,
          "end": 145.82999999999998,
          "en": "And such a key can be created by using the built-in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.82999999999998,
          "end": 149.04,
          "en": "ValueKey constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.04,
          "end": 152.73,
          "en": "This creates a key object, which can be used as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.73,
          "end": 154.92000000000002,
          "en": "for this key parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.92000000000002,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "And as mentioned, for most widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 159.57,
          "en": "you don't need to set any keys,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.57,
          "end": 162.84,
          "en": "you don't need to worry about keys at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.84,
          "end": 165.63,
          "en": "But here for the Dismissible widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.63,
          "end": 169.2,
          "en": "a key is needed to make sure that the correct data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.2,
          "end": 170.28300000000002,
          "en": "will be deleted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.02,
          "end": 173.57999999999998,
          "en": "So here we must create such a key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.57999999999998,
          "end": 175.98,
          "en": "and ValueKey wants an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.98,
          "end": 178.65,
          "en": "in the end it wants some input that can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.65,
          "end": 182.43,
          "en": "as a unique identification criteria",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.43,
          "end": 186.42,
          "en": "or value for the widget to which the key is attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.42,
          "end": 187.65,
          "en": "And in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.65,
          "end": 191.7,
          "en": "we could simply take our expense identified by index",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.7,
          "end": 194.22,
          "en": "as a value for ValueKey,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.22,
          "end": 197.01,
          "en": "and that's all we have to do regarding that key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.01,
          "end": 202.01,
          "en": "With that, if we add a comma for formatting and save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.05,
          "end": 204.03,
          "en": "and maybe force a reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.03,
          "end": 208.59,
          "en": "you will see that you can now swipe those list items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.59,
          "end": 210.66,
          "en": "and this then removes them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.66,
          "end": 215.1,
          "en": "Now the connected data is actually not removed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.1,
          "end": 219.27,
          "en": "therefore, if I add a new item here real quick,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.27,
          "end": 223.62,
          "en": "a new expense, you will see that I get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.62,
          "end": 225.9,
          "en": "basically because we have a mismatch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.9,
          "end": 227.73,
          "en": "between what's showing on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 227.73,
          "end": 231.48,
          "en": "and which data is still stored internally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.48,
          "end": 235.74,
          "en": "But this is generally how you get this swiping effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 235.74,
          "end": 239.25,
          "en": "Now of course, we must make sure that we also do something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 239.25,
          "end": 242.34,
          "en": "when we swiped a widget away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 242.34,
          "end": 246.06,
          "en": "And for that, you can add the onDismissed parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.06,
          "end": 248.76,
          "en": "which allows you to trigger a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 248.76,
          "end": 251.91,
          "en": "whenever one widget has been swiped away,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 251.91,
          "end": 254.43,
          "en": "so when it has been dismissed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 254.43,
          "end": 257.16,
          "en": "And here I of course wanna trigger a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 257.16,
          "end": 260.16,
          "en": "which then removes the associated data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 260.16,
          "end": 263.4,
          "en": "from my list of expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 263.4,
          "end": 266.55,
          "en": "So I wanna update the registeredExpenses list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.55,
          "end": 269.973,
          "en": "whenever I swiped one of my expense items away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 271.5,
          "end": 276,
          "en": "Therefore, we should go to the expenses dart file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276,
          "end": 278.19,
          "en": "to the ExpensesState, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 278.19,
          "end": 281.88,
          "en": "where we also added addExpense before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 281.88,
          "end": 284.13,
          "en": "and add another method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 284.13,
          "end": 287.43,
          "en": "And this other method could be called removeExpense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 287.43,
          "end": 289.38,
          "en": "because that is what I want to do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 290.7,
          "end": 294.6,
          "en": "And in the end here, I want to get the expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 294.6,
          "end": 299.047,
          "en": "that should be removed, and we can then call setState here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 300.33,
          "end": 303.393,
          "en": "and reach out to the registeredExpenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 305.1,
          "end": 308.85,
          "en": "And there, call remove and pass the expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 308.85,
          "end": 311.043,
          "en": "that should be removed as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 312.21,
          "end": 314.19,
          "en": "And that should make sure that the expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 314.19,
          "end": 317.49,
          "en": "is not just removed visually from the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 317.49,
          "end": 320.61,
          "en": "but also internally from that list of expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 320.61,
          "end": 321.573,
          "en": "that we managed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 323.16,
          "end": 327.15,
          "en": "Now in expenses_list, we must accept this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 327.15,
          "end": 330.48,
          "en": "as an input so that we can call this removeExpense function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 330.48,
          "end": 331.803,
          "en": "from inside this widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 332.7,
          "end": 334.89,
          "en": "Therefore, as we did it multiple times before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 334.89,
          "end": 338.13,
          "en": "in this course already, we can add a new property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 338.13,
          "end": 341.19,
          "en": "which actually wants a function that returns nothing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 341.19,
          "end": 344.943,
          "en": "but that takes an expense as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 346.23,
          "end": 350.013,
          "en": "and that could be called onRemoveExpense here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 351.65999999999997,
          "end": 353.28,
          "en": "And of course, this must be set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 353.28,
          "end": 355.98,
          "en": "when the expenses_list widget is created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 355.98,
          "end": 359.73,
          "en": "So, we require it and then bind the named",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 359.73,
          "end": 363.873,
          "en": "onRemoveExpense parameter to this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 365.07,
          "end": 366.63,
          "en": "And therefore, of course, down here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 366.63,
          "end": 368.88,
          "en": "we can execute this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 368.88,
          "end": 372.18,
          "en": "However, we can't point at it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 372.18,
          "end": 376.11,
          "en": "because on dismissed actually wants a function as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 376.11,
          "end": 380.34,
          "en": "that takes a so-called DismissDirection as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 380.34,
          "end": 382.8,
          "en": "which simply is some information that tells us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 382.8,
          "end": 386.49,
          "en": "whether we swiped from left to right or right to left,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 386.49,
          "end": 389.97,
          "en": "so that you could in theory do different things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 389.97,
          "end": 392.043,
          "en": "depending on how the user swiped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 393.36,
          "end": 396.09000000000003,
          "en": "Now here all simply set us to an anonymous function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 396.09000000000003,
          "end": 398.4,
          "en": "therefore where I get this direction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 398.4,
          "end": 401.01,
          "en": "and I'm not really interested in the direction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 401.01,
          "end": 403.8,
          "en": "but I still have to accept it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 403.8,
          "end": 406.433,
          "en": "And then I can call onRemoveExpense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 407.73,
          "end": 412.73,
          "en": "and then pass my expense as a value to onRemoveExpense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 413.55,
          "end": 417.12,
          "en": "and basically ignore this direction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 417.12,
          "end": 419.88,
          "en": "Well, and with that, we just have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 419.88,
          "end": 423.42,
          "en": "that removeExpense is also passed as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 423.42,
          "end": 425.49,
          "en": "to ExpensesList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 425.49,
